{"qid":"Q928","names":["Republic of the Philippines"],"title":"Republic of the Philippines","endonym":{"native":"Philippines","lang":"en"},"capsule":"The Republic of the Philippines, proclaimed independent on July 4, 1946, is an archipelago state of over 7,600 islands in Southeast Asia, successor to the Commonwealth of the Philippines under American tutelage since 1935. Its postwar political trajectory included the Huk rebellion of the late 1940s–1950s, Ferdinand Marcos's declaration of martial law in 1972, the People Power Revolution of February 1986 that restored civilian democracy under Corazon Aquino, and continued governance through successive elected administrations into the twenty-first century. The country's economy grew substantially from the 1990s onward, driven by remittances and business-process outsourcing, though recurring challenges of corruption, insurgency in Mindanao, and typhoon vulnerability persisted.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The Philippines' territorial extent as an archipelago is precisely documented through modern statehood, though exact maritime boundary claims remain disputed with neighboring states.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Philippines","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippines"},{"label":"Wikipedia: History of the Philippines (1946–1965)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_the_Philippines_(1946%E2%80%931965)"},{"label":"Wikipedia: People Power Revolution","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People_Power_Revolution"}],"britannica":"place/Philippines","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Philippines","rulers":[{"qid":"Q223419","name":"M